course: dictionary
lesson: 9650
title: Subheadings: signposts inside a text
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A subheading is a smaller heading under the main heading of a text. It tells you what one section is about, like a signpost on a path that shows what is coming up next.
explain: «In non-fiction, headings, subheadings and signposts such as "Firstly, secondly, finally" organise the text.» Headings and subheadings split a text into parts, so you know where to look.
explain: Use subheadings to skim, which means reading quickly to find the part you need. If you want to know what a bird eats, look for the subheading «Diet» and skip the rest of the text.
fact: A subheading is a smaller heading under the main heading.
fact: A subheading tells you what the section below it is about.
fact: Common subheadings in a report about an animal are «Habitat», «Diet» and «Life cycle».
fact: «Sub-» means under, as in «subheading» and «submarine».
fact: Subheadings are part of how a text is organised, so they help you find facts quickly.
exercise: What is a subheading? | The last sentence of a text | A picture with a caption | The title of the whole book | *A smaller heading under the main heading, telling you what a section is about
exercise: The word «subheading» starts with the prefix sub-. What does sub- mean? | *Under | Again | Wrongly | Two
exercise: A report about frogs has the subheadings «Habitat», «Diet» and «Life cycle». Which subheading would help you find what frogs eat? | Habitat | Summary | *Diet | Life cycle
test: Why do writers use subheadings in non-fiction? | To replace every sentence in the text | *To help the reader skim and find facts quickly | To hide the main heading | To make the text longer and harder to read
test: Which prefix means under, as in «submarine»? | tri- | bi- | *sub- | re-
exam: A non-fiction text has the main heading «Owls» and the subheading «Habitat». Where would you look to find out where owls live? | *In the section under «Habitat» | In the title of the book | Nowhere, because subheadings never show facts | In the section under «Diet»
